===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*haliþaz||man, hero}}, further etymology unknown.

Cognate with Old High German {{m|goh|helid}} (German {{m|de|Held}}), Old Saxon {{m|osx|helid}}, Old Dutch {{m|odt|helt}} (Dutch {{m|nl|held}}), West Frisian {{m|fy|held}}, Old Norse {{m|non|halr}}, {{m|non|hǫlðr}} (Norwegian {{m|no|hold}}, Swedish {{m|se|hjälte}}). The Indo-European root is also the source of Ancient Greek {{m|grc|κελωρ}}, Tocharian B {{m|txb||kālyśke|boy}}.

